                            {
                                "example_id": "cf500275-d9fe-461b-8345-0c0a781b53e4",
                                "sense_id": "25dec137-31f8-31b7-b05a-cc7611ff75e7",
                                "text": "„In Mexiko-Stadt ist eine der größten Mülldeponien der Welt geschlossen worden.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c1230004-8687-40ef-949a-82ff9bcf7dc3",
                        "source_entry_id": "b076c65e-d5a9-38da-9e73-15aa811de4ac",
                        "source_sense_id": "25dec137-31f8-31b7-b05a-cc7611ff75e7",
                        "source_sense_description": "Hauptstadt von Mexiko",
                        "target_lang_word": "Mexico City",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Mexico City",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "70f9a5a8-8e19-32fb-8e47-eb21651dd5c5",
                                        "entry_id": "b0d70cd4-c1c5-3873-9ba1-09d2b7a23ce2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The capital city of Mexico."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba892ab6-33a8-4c51-b3a6-e94cc87f8e3f",
                                                "sense_id": "70f9a5a8-8e19-32fb-8e47-eb21651dd5c5",
                                                "text": "I went to Mexico City on April 15, 1966, to unveil a statue of Abraham Lincoln, who had been a contemporary of Mexican leader Benito Juarez and was revered in Mexico, as in so many other nations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7db6ad2-4ce2-4ac5-89f6-983c26b27ee6",
                                                "sense_id": "70f9a5a8-8e19-32fb-8e47-eb21651dd5c5",
                                                "text": "The writer Juan Rulfo, whose 1955 novel, “Pedro Páramo,” still stands as the central monument of modern Mexican literature, grew up in Jalisco and vividly depicted its arid, sun-blasted landscapes in his writing, while the architect Luis Barragán, who moved from Guadalajara to Mexico City in the 1930s, carried with him an appreciation for his home state’s cloisters, haciendas and humble country buildings, which he translated in his own work as austere, inscrutable volumes of stucco."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "93c8b3f1-00e7-49e6-a02d-22d2baf8139d",
                        "source_entry_id": "b076c65e-d5a9-38da-9e73-15aa811de4ac",
                        "source_sense_id": "25dec137-31f8-31b7-b05a-cc7611ff75e7",
                        "source_sense_description": "Hauptstadt von Mexiko",
                        "target_lang_word": "Mexico",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Mexico",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "85c8519c-c883-3d39-95fc-1e972b69b498",
                                        "entry_id": "d436f4e0-caa0-391f-a797-4907dcaac6a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ville du Mexique dont le nom officiel est Ciudad de México (« Ville de Mexico »). C’est la capitale du pays et l’une des plus grandes villes du monde. La ville compte 8,605,239 habitants (2000) mais l’agglomération compte plus de 18,000,000 d’habitants (2006) et s’étend sur plus de 1,500 km²."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3cf43499-a831-4d04-bfa7-e7e5f84e4dae",
                                                "sense_id": "85c8519c-c883-3d39-95fc-1e972b69b498",
                                                "text": "Ça tombe bien : El Padrino marche à voile et à vapeur, et ce sont, semble-t-il, des copains de son milieu qui lui dégotent en 1983 un emploi de top-model masculin à Mexico, capitale fédérale."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dab31d40-21f7-46b0-966c-9b696e9d8976",
                                                "sense_id": "85c8519c-c883-3d39-95fc-1e972b69b498",
                                                "text": "La ville de Mexico a été construite sur les ruines de Tenochtitlan, capitale de l’empire Aztèque."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2f5d4a56-4384-3414-81d3-17eaae6761f4",
                                        "entry_id": "d436f4e0-caa0-391f-a797-4907dcaac6a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "État de Mexico."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
